"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2841,"Narrated to us Qays ibn ar-Rabīʿ, on the authority of al-Agharr, from Khālifah ibn Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAlī (RA), who said:
""The most frequent supplication of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) during the evening of ʿArafah was:

**'Allāhumma laka al-ḥamdu ka-lladhī naqūlu wa khayran mimmā naqūl. Allāhumma laka ṣalātī wa nusukī, wa maḥyāya wa mamātī, ilayka maʾābī, wa laka rabbī tarāʾī.**

**Allāhumma innī aʿūdhu bika min ʿadhābi al-qabr, wa waswāsati aṣ-ṣadr, wa shatāti al-amr.**

**Allāhumma innī asʾaluka min khayri mā tajīʾu bihi ar-riyāḥ, wa aʿūdhu bika min sharri mā tajīʾu bihi ar-riyāḥ.'**

Translation:
'O Allāh, to You is all praise, such as we say and better than what we say. O Allāh, to You is my prayer, my rites of devotion, my life and my death, and to You is my return. You are my Lord, and I see You.'

'O Allāh, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, from the whisperings of the chest, and from the disarray of affairs.

'O Allāh, I ask You for the good that the wind brings, and I seek refuge in You from the evil that the wind brings.'""

---
**CHAPTER:**"
